drafts.tidy:
Beware — my blade of fire is wielded with daring, my thunderous roar upon the field of fame, so fierce as the moon’s own sigh,
I am fearless, unbound by gloom, while shadows whisper doubts in crypt;
Thus do I stand, the goddess of war, to break the night, and let it tremble before my name’s own fury—beware.

plays.verse:
Giovanna! Tu che bramante spada al sole,
Se ti ferisci, e il mio cuore ti chiede troppo;
Chi sei? Chi è quel malvivente che ti sfida?

