I raise not the blade, but silence keeps the peace,
Put up thy sword and let me show the score;
Peace is my shield, yet you wield the steel at your stride.

plays.verse:
Fear not, I say, with pugnale held high,
My voice is steel and fire within my sight;
Put up thy sword, or taste the blood.

